# Withdrawn from the public site 2026-08-12 — kept in git, not deployed.
# The cryptography explainer is unaudited (see the landing copy audit) and is
# Russian-only on an English-default site. Restore by deleting these three lines,
# the redirect in vercel.json, and un-commenting the demo card in faq.html.
crypto.html
crypto.css
crypto.js

# `package.json` exists so `npm run dev` starts the local preview server. It is
# not part of the site, and Vercel must not see it: an uploaded package.json is
# what turns a static project into one with an install/build step, which is
# exactly what this project does not have. Keeping it out of the upload leaves
# the deployment byte-identical to before the file existed.
package.json
package-lock.json
node_modules
